s":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I approve PKT-0016. The goal is met: the server now runs, and `baseline.md` has a real breakdown of open time and co-edit delay for Word, spreadsheet and presentation samples, with the raw results committed. I checked the tables against the raw results file and they match.\n\n**Rejection conditions (TEP-0004):** none applies.\n- The Executor log is full, attempt 8 included.\n- The one follow-up (put the install recipe into `environment.md`) is committed under `.theseus/spawn/`.\n- This is an investigate packet, not a characterize one, so the rule that every surprise must be kept in a test does not apply. The surprises are written in the log and in `baseline.md`.\n\n**Contract and budget:** both are respected.\n- No project source code changed; `client-perf.js` is untouched.\n- The diff touches 6 files with about 275 added lines, against limits of 6 files and 800 lines.\n- The friction line is recorded in `friction.jsonl`.\n\n**Weak points that should not block approval:**\n1. **One sentence overstates the data.** `baseline.md` says the receiver's apply time is \"larger on the big document\". That holds for p50 (73 vs 42 ms) and max (187 vs 155 ms), but not for p90, where the big document is faster (105 vs 143 ms).\n2. **\"Cold HTTP cache\" is probably not true for every open.** Several runs report about 0–8 KB of scripts transferred instead of about 500 KB. That includes the first presentation open, which was also the first file measured. So scripts seem to come from a cache or are under-reported. The \"~1.5 s for scripts\" figure may mix cold and warm loads.\n3. **The co-edit split is approximate.** The script uses the first outgoing and incoming change message. 9 of the 60 edits sent two messages, so their batching and network shares are approximate. Edits that time out become NaN and are silently dropped from the percentiles. None were lost in this run, since every sample count is 30.\n4. **Only 3 opens per file.** Its p90 is the same as its maximum, so the open numbers show direction, not stable percentiles. The \"CPU contention\" explanation for PKT-0015's slow worst cases is an inference, and the log presents it as one.\n5. **The x2t conversion time is still not measured separately.** This is declared and moved to the Gaps table with a concrete follow-up (server-side timestamps), which is acceptable for an investigate packet.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Goal met with real open and co-edit breakdowns on four document types; contract and budget respected; follow-up spawned; only minor wording and cache caveats","ttft_ms":2388,"type":"result","duration_ms":23412,"uuid":"bc915fad-f40b-45d6-861e-c4c4d38c5d5a","ttft_stream_ms":1101,"time_to_request_ms":401,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":196,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":26,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":48,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":26,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":16,"model_gates":2,"tool_schema_build":28,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":3,"request_build":9},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":113,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":281,"time_to_request_major_faults":2,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":224,"process_anon_mib_result":135,"process_peak_rss_mib":238,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1141,"process_wall_ms_turn":23412,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":448,"process_wall_ms_streaming":19818,"main_stream_count":5,"main_stream_event_count":319,"main_stream_chunk_count":119,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":11,"cpu_ms":24,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":9,"ambient_wait_ms":10,"render_ms":3,"produ